  "cover_text": "The court system in Sheridan, Arkansas is a government branch made up of judges responsible for three categories of cases: civil, criminal, and treason. It is governed by the Sheridan-Young County Circuit Court Judges Supervising Council, which is composed of Circuit Court Judges. The auditor reports to the circuit court to assess its financial records. Due to the jurisdiction of the Sheridan-Young County Circuit Court, it must have special jurisdiction, with jurisdiction over the two principal constitutional subjects of individual rights and state government. The Sheridan-Young County Circuit Court has an appellate jurisdiction. Legal counsel for the Supreme Court sitting here in court is Sirvikhana Sunyish, an assistant solicitor of justices.\n\nSummary:\n\nThe judges are responsible for three distinct",
